From: Starch Linux Project
Subject: [PATCH] Skip OS probing in the erase-only installer

Starch does not support sharing a disk with an existing installation. Avoid
probing or temporarily mounting other systems just to label the erase page.
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Starch-specific installer policy]
License: GPL-3.0-or-later
--- a/src/modules/partition/core/PartitionCoreModule.cpp
+++ b/src/modules/partition/core/PartitionCoreModule.cpp
@@ -293,7 +293,7 @@
 
     // The following PartUtils::runOsprober call in turn calls PartUtils::canBeResized,
     // which relies on a working DeviceModel.
-    m_osproberLines = PartUtils::runOsprober( this->deviceModel() );
+    m_osproberLines.clear(); // Whole-disk erase needs no existing-OS discovery.
 
     // We perform a best effort of filling out filesystem UUIDs in m_osproberLines
     // because we will need them later on in PartitionModel if partition paths
